    {
      "id": "KlEe-4sYeXI6rtFt-3Upo",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -6.898994764194072,
      "y": -43.78266712250144,
      "width": 715.579345703125,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aA",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 235430483,
      "version": 546,
      "versionNonce": 1986595699,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1791304284934,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "a couple starting points...\n\n[1] how fast does this have to run? we get ~66.5mhz CLK from RP2040\n        [a] does one bit have to be sent in 4 instructions? 8? 1?\n[2] how much data do we have to receive/store at once?\n        [a] how do we say we are \"busy\" or not ready? \n        [b] how fast do we have to send this back to the RP2040/host?\n     ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "a couple starting points...\n\n[1] how fast does this have to run? we get ~66.5mhz CLK from RP2040\n        [a] does one bit have to be sent in 4 instructions? 8? 1?\n[2] how much data do we have to receive/store at once?\n        [a] how do we say we are \"busy\" or not ready? \n        [b] how fast do we have to send this back to the RP2040/host?\n     ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
